id: pm-ts-starter-relative-package-identity
title: Support relative local packages with compiler-owned identities
description: "Follow-up to PR 154. Relative declarations across nested local package boundaries and some classic typesVersions subpaths lack a Program packageId. Preserve typed refusals until ownership is available from compiler resolution data, without synthetic imports, independent resolution or package metadata ancestry. Ordinary local declarations, unused metadata and compiler-identified installed dependencies remain supported. Project references are refused separately and tracked by pm-ts-starter-project-references."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: compatibility,compiler-api,follow-up
created_at: "2026-10-27T19:39:58.222Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T16:38:16.633Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Obtain ownership from actual Program resolution data without synthetic imports or package metadata ancestry; retain current typed refusal until identity is available; preserve direct compiler diagnostics and exact installed layouts; include named, unnamed, nested and mts/cts/ts package fixtures"
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T16:30:53.920Z",codex-agent,"Round 14 removes the referenced-project exemption entirely: references are now unsupported and tracked separately by pm-ts-starter-project-references. Native TypeScript 5.9.3 also returns resolvedFileName and isExternalLibraryImport but no packageId for the typesVersions subpath fixture in test/sdk-program-graph.test.ts. Retain isolation_refused there and unsupported_project_shape for unidentified relative local packages. The dependency corpus retains the original relative workspace fixture as a refusal and adds an installed-name workspace control. Future support must obtain a compiler-owned identity without synthesizing resolution or walking metadata ancestry."
